&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Luna-Kelreader: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/place-kel/luna. Handback to
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/place-kel/luna/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 1000 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. No git writes, no suites. Web allowed.
Code: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine (span head 43bdc025f, K15 Wave D landed, read only).

WAVE TWO. Common brief: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/place-kel/brief-common.md. Your wave one: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/place-kel/luna/own-wave1.md. Your peer's: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/place-kel/luna/peer-wave1.md.

You agree: one KEL grammar (persona/handle patterns reused), place-specific authority, no interaction events; road:207
rules the online scoped signer, the offline next key on the founding card, rotation by the card, re-found when card and
signer both fall, TPM-bound where offered and an owner-only file otherwise; framing changes four duties' bytes and rides
X0 behind a readiness red, signer and verifiers together. Settle the kit's edges:

K1. THE SEED'S OTHER REACH. You both found the place seed signing more than the five duties: the place ContactCard and
archive (place-card.ts), leaf-identity.ts, relay, daemon auth, internal asks, device and face work
(open-node-vessel.ts:981,1447,2283,3451). Road :208 names some as bonds owed and carried by K15. MEASURE at the span
head (Wave D landed) which still read the seed. Sort each: (i) a place duty that joins the scoped signer (a sixth
domain? the card and the KEL itself sign by which key?), (ii) a face or device principal that belongs to K15's
owed bonds (name the row), (iii) dead. The lane must NOT swallow K15's bonds; it must leave the seed reaching
nothing outside its list, with a census red proving it (silent-zero, planted positive).
K2. THE CARD CEREMONY. Rotation reveals the card's key and commits a fresh next key: where does the NEW next key rest
(a new card written in the same ceremony, read back before the event lands, as cofound.ts and seal-ceremony.ts
rehearse)? Torn landing: the event lands but the card write fails, or the reverse; name the order that re-enters
to one end. Measure cofound.ts's cold-card read-back and say what reuses.
K3. PEERS LEARN THE NEW HEAD. Who carries the rotation to peers that pinned the inception (the Nexus carriage board,
the floor porch, the herm)? Which existing board carries public place records? How a reader that pinned only the
inception verifies descent. Keep W14–W16's claim lane separate: this lane delivers the KEL and its readers.
K4. GENESIS AND FIXTURES. Every founding mints the new inception (with next digest) and the founding card carries the
next key: list the founding paths (node found, hearth, cofound, herm stand) and test fixtures that mint a place
today, and how they migrate through the real founding path, never a hand-built fixture.
K5. THE FINAL KIT: slices in order, files held, every red with its control and known positive, the readiness red for X0,
overlap contracts (K17-R, W28 owns gate-exchange where gate-place-finish lives, W26), and any question that still
survives as truly the operator's (options, lean), or say none survives.

